Structure
Grandparent → Parent → Child

Step 1 — First Class
class Animal 
{
    void eat() 
    {
        System.out.println("Eating");
    }
}

Step 2 — Second Class Inherits First
class Dog extends Animal 
{
    void bark() 
    {
        System.out.println("Barking");
    }
}

Step 3 — Third Class Inherits Second
class Puppy extends Dog 
{
    void weep() 
    {
        System.out.println("Weeping");
    }
}

Step 4 — Main Method
public class Main 
{
    public static void main(String[] args) 
   {
        Puppy p = new Puppy();
        p.eat();
        p.bark();
        p.weep();
    }
}

Output :
Eating
Barking
Weeping
